	MAKE AND RECEIVE A CALL

1.) Check the headphone with speakers with modem attached to a computer if the mic works.
1a.)The butons can be hardware debounced if the debouncing code in risc-v is too long.

2.) We need to write a code in risc-v that boots up the machine and polls (or interrupts)
	the GPIO for buttons and USART2 for the 4G modem.

3.)	We need to send out a predefined number in the AT command to make a call

4.)	We need to make the phone ring/or display a number or both and assign two GPIOs
	to receive and end a call

5.)	Add the funcionality to dial a number from the phone.





We have 8 input buttons hardware debounced with capacitors.
Five of which are for inputting soroban style numbers.
	# Two buttons on each side are manipulated with the thumbs
	# and the the two on each side with i and m.
	# right outer button pressed with the thumb is for the upper pebble and
	# the left and right i and m for the lower four pebbles in the soroban
	# zero is pressed with the right hand m.

	# The right inner button is for enter/receive call
	# The left inner button is for esc/end call
	# The left outer button is to toggle between vocabularies (like in FORTH) and menues
	# Maybe I will swap the thumb button functions (outer buttons for esc/enter) 
	# So basically it is a 8 bit input device that is ntered uppon releasing
	# all the buttons so I have 256 commands times the number of vocabularies.

The numbers are presented on the led matrix wheather incoming or outgoing call.
The numbers can be later be aliased to a name.


The storage for the code is not going to be in the blocks it should fit on the FLASH. 
But the "filesystem" for data (SD card ove SPI) should be organised so that the root
is a person`s name and in that block are defined allocatins (lines) for phone number SMS and call logs. Missed calls should also be a sort of block
